ed."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Shape & Layer: Key Lime Pie"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"When you are ready to serve, carefully remove the pie from the tin and put on a serving plate. To decorate, softly whip together the cream and icing sugar. Dollop or pipe the cream onto the top of the pie and finish with extra lime zest."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Cool Completely, Garnish & Serve"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Transfer Key Lime Pie to a wire cooling rack and let it cool for 15–20 minutes so the interior sets cleanly without crumbling. Lift out using the parchment overhang, garnish as desired, and slice into 6 portions."}]]}]]}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","viral-15",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/no-bake-salted-caramel-banoffee-pie/","children":"No-Bake Salted Caramel Banoffee Pie"}]}],["$","li","viral-21",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/portuguese-pastel-de-nata-custard-tarts/","children":"Portuguese Pastel de Nata Custard Tarts"}]}],["$","li","mdb-52893",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-blackberry-crumble/","children":"Apple & Blackberry Crumble"}]}],["$","li","mdb-52768",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-frangipan-tart/","children":"Apple Frangipan Tart"}]}],["$","li","mdb-53575",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-pie/","children":"Apple Pie"}]}],["$","li","mdb-53568",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/apple-pie-pops/","children":"Apple pie pops"}]}]]}]]}]}]
